    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on aggressive upside, headlined by **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.72) and **Mickey Moniak** (69.85). **Tyler Soderstrom** is our strongest play, benefitting significantly from a favorable matchup against Kelly (5.31 xERA) and an elevated position in the batting order. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** leverages a massive 14% park factor boost and a strong platoon advantage to anchor our outfield output. We are also leaning heavily on **James Wood** (69.20), whose elite 0.425 xwOBA and lead-off spot make him an essential engine for our scoring, even as he faces a respectable arm in Hughes.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was excluding **Josh Naylor** (59.33) from the starting lineup. While his score is respectable, he ultimately fell short due to poor historical BvP metrics (28 PA) and a negative park factor against Singer. Conversely, we are riding with **Jose Caballero** (64.63) over other options; despite his dynamic platoon risk, the wind blowing out at the stadium and his high SP skill coefficient against Keller make him too efficient to sit, particularly given his value in our scarce stolen base category. \n\nWe are monitoring several risk factors closely. **Corbin Carroll** (58.95) and **Gabriel Moreno** (51.50) face Jump, a lefty who presents a notable challenge for our left-handed bats, causing a drag on their base projections. Furthermore, we\u2019ve flagged wind-in conditions for **Seiya Suzuki** and **Vinnie Pasquantino**; while both remain in the starting lineup due to their strong offensive ceilings, those atmospheric conditions necessitate a cautious outlook on their power output today. We have relegated **Edwin Arroyo** to the bench, as his projection of 38.90 sits safely below our 40.0 efficiency floor.",
